# Gameplay reproduction for inc-p0h1 (Bestow Curse redesign), the PLAYER
# MENU code path this bead adds -- only reachable on the branch build --
# picking the SECOND of its three curses: a -4 penalty to attack rolls,
# saving throws and skill checks. Sibling of
# tools/keys/bestow-curse-menu-ability.keys; see that file's header for the
# wizard-mode setup this one repeats.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/bestow-curse-menu-misfortune.keys 1
#
# The goblin's own Dump() (wizard "Examine Nearby Things") is read before and
# after: A_HIT and the three A_SAV_* rows should each read four lower, with
# a "SS_CURS" breakdown line naming "bestow curse" -- the skill penalty
# (SKILL_BONUS,SK_ANY) has no line in Creature::Dump's fixed PrintAttr table
# (src/Debug.cpp:1414), so it is not something this screen can show; only
# the saves and to-hit are checked here.

@include chargen-priest.keys
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Bestow Curse"
ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:goblin-summoned

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
RIGHT
@dump:goblin-before
ESC

m
@choose "Bestow Curse"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:curse-menu

@choose "a -4 penalty to attacks, saves and skills"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:cast-misfortune

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
RIGHT
@dump:goblin-after
ESC

v
@dump:message-log
@while "Messages" ESC

@quit
